  "scope": "# Review: 0b8ba9bb3c63, version 4.0.0 \u2192 4.1.0\n\nAcceptance: routine for the canonical repair; the separate beam-axis extension remains an unapproved prototype.\nDefect \u2192 repair: public-only demonstrations hid non-blue blocking; a five-position 2:3 public/generalized schedule now supplies observable non-blue shadows.\nFinal generator SHA-256: `480c7ae04f31b1cd2d48c8b4af0dd9f71ef9365507a557c9fc6d60cb44ddc20d`.\nReference rule: unchanged `757441c9ab4a`; two selected authority copies received exact-text formatting synchronization only; archival raw text is unchanged.\nStrict after battery: 12/12 green, 0 advisory, 0 failed; baseline was 9 green, 1 advisory, 2 failed.\nLessons: three ordered demonstrations then one query; 300/300 production lessons and 1,200/1,200 held-out query rotations refute the declared blue-only rival.\nSchedule: all five start residues at seed 0 across three bands pass\u201415 production lessons, 60 rotations, 60 pair occurrences, 16 distinct inputs.\nPortable tests: 61 tests plus 49 subtests pass (110 JUnit cases); no failures, errors, or skips.\nPrototype: `beam_axes \u2208 {both, horizontal, vertical}`; 9/9 production episodes and 36/36 query rotations distinguish the declared alternatives using actual Racket outputs.\nFresh replay: 15/15 changed-file hashes match; independent-environment rerun passes 61 tests plus 49 subtests; remaining canonical-repair blockers: none.\nLimits: finite rival inventory and sampled geometry; ordinary lesson guarantee requires consecutive successful draws; both peer audits remain findings-only.\n",
